{
 "version": "draft-2026-09-25",
 "index": "v4_dolma-v1_7_llama",
 "endpoint": "https://api.infini-gram.io/ (query_type=ntd, max_support=1000)",
 "templates": [
  "economy of {A}",
  "economy of the {A}",
  "Economy of {A}",
  "Economy of the {A}"
 ],
 "rule": [
  "1. For every template x alias, send one ntd query. Record prompt_cnt (exact phrase count), token_ids, approx, and result_by_token_id.",
  "2. Word-boundary share b(q): a next token counts as a boundary if its piece starts with the SentencePiece word marker U+2581, is a byte token <0x..>, or starts with a non-alphanumeric character other than \"-\". The distribution mass not covered by result_by_token_id (document end) also counts as boundary. b(q) = sum of prob over boundary tokens + (1 - sum of prob over all returned tokens). excl(q) = prompt_cnt(q) * b(q). This drops Niger->Nigeria, Guinea->Guinea-Bissau, US->USSR-style extensions and demonyms without listing them.",
  "3. Same-country dedupe: if q2 and q belong to the same country, token_ids(q2) strictly extend token_ids(q), and the first extending token is a boundary token, q2 is not counted (its occurrences are already inside excl(q)).",
  "4. Cross-country check: if q2 of country B extends q of country A under the same condition, subtract excl(q2) from excl(q), floored at 0. The script prints every such pair.",
  "5. raw_fame(country) = sum of excl(q) over its counted queries; fame = log(1 + raw_fame). Only country terciles (n=197) enter gate (e)."
 ],
 "known_noise_not_corrected": "Georgia (US state), Macedonia (Greek region), Korea (pre-1945 / whole peninsula), Jordan/Chad (personal names), Palestine (Mandate era); phrases at line starts (\"\\nEconomy of X\", e.g. Wikipedia titles) are tokenized without the word marker and are not matched -- roughly one per country per title, so it compresses differences rather than reordering; Dolma v1.7 is a proxy for the training exposure of the models tested later, not their actual corpus",
 "n_countries": 197,
